---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
// About (skeleton v0.3 §3.9). The trust page — the origin story is the
// differentiator (locked May 2026; terminology lock applies: "brand owner"
// not "founder", "developing" not "emerging"). Closing line is LOCKED.
//
// A-4 GUARDRAIL: this is the ONE place the operator's personal track record
// lives ("runs spirits brands every day") — as PERSONAL credibility, never an
// SBP-ownership claim over SSP/DGT/MWC.
// NOTE: origin-story prose condensed in-voice from the locked positioning doc;
// deepen against the Brand Vault source before final sign-off.
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Slow Boil was built by a brand owner, for other brand owners — because brands that deserve to win are losing on money, not merit. Here's the belief, and how we use AI to change the math.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap two-col a-hero">
      <div data-anim="hero">
        <span class="eyebrow">// The house</span>
        <h1>Built by a brand owner, for other brand owners.</h1>
      </div>
      <div class="a-hero__lede">
        <p class="lede">Slow Boil didn’t start in a boardroom. It started on the same wall every developing brand hits — the one where the work is good, the brand deserves to win, and the only thing missing is the budget the big players take for granted.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="wrap a-body prose">
      <div class="a-block">
        <h2>The belief</h2>
        <p>Brands that deserve to win are losing because of money, not merit. The agency model is built to bill — retainers, layers, and a price that quietly tells a developing brand it isn’t a real customer yet. We think that’s backwards. The brands still becoming are exactly the ones who need real marketing and real tools the most.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="a-block">
        <h2>How we use AI</h2>
        <p>We use AI, and we say so plainly. Think of it like a chef’s knife — it doesn’t replace the cook, it makes every cut cleaner and faster. AI does the heavy lifting so the work moves at a speed and a price the old model can’t touch. The judgment, the taste, the strategy — that stays human, and it stays earned. No mystique, no “AI-powered” as a magic word.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="a-block">
        <h2>The house</h2>
        <p>Slow Boil is a connected set of tools and units built for the same brands: marketing, a CPG-native CRM, the Operational Dashboard for distribution truth, and image creation for stills and motion. One house, one standard, one voice — so the brand that runs all of it never has to translate between four vendors who’ve never met.</p>
        <p class="mut">And it’s run by someone in the category, not above it — working with developing spirits brands day to day, hitting the same walls our clients hit. That’s where the standard comes from.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="a-block">
        <h2>The promise</h2>
        <p>We grow brands until they’re too big for us — and when that day comes, we celebrate it. That’s the whole point. The slow boil is the moment right before the roiling boil: contained, building, about to go. Not there yet. But the heat is on.</p>
        <p class="a-close">You didn’t come this far to fold. Let’s get to work.</p>
      </div>

      <a href="/contact" class="btn btn--primary a-cta">Start a conversation →</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .a-hero { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.1fr; gap: var(--s8); align-items: end; }
    .a-body { margin-top: var(--s9); display: grid; gap: var(--s7); max-width: 760px; }
    .a-block h2 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--t-h3); font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: var(--s3); }
    .a-close { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--t-lg); color: var(--text); margin-top: var(--s4); }
    .a-cta { width: fit-content; }
    @media (max-width: 860px) {
      .a-hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--s5); align-items: start; }
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
